  "initial_setup_correction": "The first driver attempted to start Python in two runtime images that do not contain it; the third correctly rejected the RPM because the project signing key was absent. The corrected driver installs the same Python/util-linux test prerequisites as CI, imports the SHA-256-pinned project key and requires an OK signature. It grants the fixture user ownership of the disposable test directory. No package test or signature check was weakened. Original failures are retained.",
